  "title": "# Build: molly-nav-submenus (Current profile) ## Brett said (verbatim, Nov 3 2026, voice) \"I want M…",
  "asked": "# Build: molly-nav-submenus (Current profile) ## Brett said (verbatim, Nov 3 2026, voice) \"I want Molly to have the console's navigation menu slide open, like when you click console, have a sub menu slide open, show its menu, and same thing for AXHub and AmberX. Have a sub menu slide open with an animation and give the navigation menu its own settings interface to control everything. The theme, the way it looks, its animation, its behavior, all that.\" Assigned agent: whoever is free (router if on main; else **Reel Rhonda**; record who). Register in the `current` profile (id `molly-nav-submenus`) + banner entry. ## Context Molly = the one-app shell (apps/molly, xLayout plugin + chrome@1 + dock engine, PRs #245/#252, live) that hosts the Console, axHub web and AmberX as frames. Read `apps/molly`, the xLayout/chrome reports and THREADS first. ## Build - s1 Molly's left navigation menu: each app entry (Console, axHub, AmberX, and any future embedded app) expands a **sub menu that slides open** with that app's own navigation (the app's nav items/screens pulled live from the embedded app's nav registry: console `console.nav` / control@1, axHub web nav, AmberX nav; via embed@ messages or the control@1 reads, no hard-coded lists). Tap an item = open that screen inside the app's frame. Nested levels supported. Active item highlighted; remembers which are open. - s2 Animation: slide/accordion/fade/push/none, duration, easing, stagger of items, chevron rotation; reduced-motion respected. - s3 **Navigation menu settings interface** (its own settings, opened from the nav's context menu 'Navigation settings' and from Settings > Plugins > Navigation): theme + colours (background, text, active, hover, sub-menu background, accents per app), fonts (family, size, weight), icons (size, show/hide), density/spacing, width (min/max, resizable, collapsible to icons), animation (as s2), behaviour (single vs multiple sub menus open, open on hover vs tap on desktop, auto-collapse, remember state, swipe to open on phone, pinned items, order of apps, hide apps). Tokens/assets only (a `nav-style` asset so it's hot-swappable), live preview, presets, reset. - s4 Make it a framework nav component so the Console's own nav and other apps can use the same sub-menu + settings (opt-in), without breaking current navs. Coordinate with the Menus plugin (smart-menus) and Toolbars plugin builds only through framework APIs. - s5 Commands declared once -> REST + MCP + CLI (get/set nav settings, open item). Tests, phone + desktop screenshots, UI Review item, report `_claude/builds/reports/molly-nav-submenus.md`, THREADS, PR, steps through the store. Commits clean and professional. Watch live: Brett can watch the screen you are changing hot-render in the console. Whenever you start work on a screen or element, run `node framework/cli/axf.mjs focus <app> [route] [css-selector] --note \"<what you are changing>\"` (apps: console-web, axhub-web, amberx-droid, walkthrough-studio, demo, framework, console, axhub-android, voicevault). Agent cap: heavy steps (pnpm/npm/vite builds, docker node:22 test runs, Playwright) share a VPS-wide lock. Run each one as `node /opt/axf/deploy/../framework/cli/agent-slots.mjs heavy -- <command>` so only a few run at once. Model switches (Brett, Nov 3 2026): a downgrade (e.g. Fable → Opus) is fine. An UPGRADE (e.g. Opus → Fable) needs Brett's approval: when you reach one, run `node apps/console-web/plugins/build-orchestrator/orchestrator.mjs request-upgrade <id> <phase>`, ask once, and stop. Never approve a model switch upgrade yourself (no `act approve` on an upgrade), never relaunch on a higher model.",
